+# Rivalry card sharing to social apps — 2026-10-19
+
+The owner requests direct sharing to WhatsApp and other social apps, and explicitly selects the designed results-card image with accompanying text. RSS01-RSS03 replaces Rivalry's Android text-only handoff with a rendered PNG plus the exact `finale_share_text()` caption through the system chooser. One Share results tap prepares the image and opens sharing. The preview offers Share again; the recipient and final Send action remain in the selected app. This implementation targets the game's Android platform. The Windows preview keeps copied text and adds Save image; a Windows native sharing chooser is not implemented.
+
+RSS01 renders the existing refined card independently at 1600×860, with actual pinned results, country/name, car and local cosmetics. The surrounding game, close button, copied status and action controls are absent from the image. The capture uses an isolated bounded viewport, warms the existing static car render, then frees its temporary window/viewport. It cancels if the owning preview disappears. The prepared PNG is cached only in that preview and capped at 4 MiB. No public results URL, new image-generation service or backend data is created.
+
+RSS02 extends the original Android adapter with `shareResults(requestId, png, text)`. The intent contains `image/png`, the stream URI and exact text, with matching ClipData and read grants. A private, non-exported, read-only `RivalryShareProvider` exposes only generated PNG files in the app's cache. Package-specific `${applicationId}` authority wiring works with the configured application ID. Unique staged writes and a six-image/24-hour cleanup policy give a 24 MiB retained-image budget; one new receipt can temporarily coexist during a save. Unknown names, traversal, foreign authorities and write access are refused. No new SDK, dependency, storage permission or external account connection is added. Existing challenge/track text sharing is retained.
+
+RSS03 coalesces repeated taps during image preparation and rechecks account/car scope, snapshot ownership, week/group, results text and navigation before native dispatch. Closing or navigating cancels late image completion. Native launch errors carry the request identity and allow retry; older errors cannot replace a newer request. The UI says Ready to share, and never treats opening/cancelling a chooser as confirmed delivery. On desktop, the Save image action uses the native save dialog, rechecks the same context and writes the generated PNG; the user chooses the file path.
+
+Changed files: `game/core/app.gd`, `game/platform/challenge_links.gd`, `game/ui/rivalry_share_dialog.gd`, new `game/ui/rivalry_share_image.gd`, `game/addons/bmt_challenges/export_plugin.gd`, `native/challenges/src/org/beatmytrack/challenges/BmtChallenges.java`, new `RivalryShareFiles.java`/`RivalryShareProvider.java`, `game/tests/test_rivalry_share.gd`, `scripts/test_track_link_bridge.py`, native provenance, the live AR09 documentation, this note and `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`. Saved originals, final sources and the [task-only patch](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/task-only.patch) are accompanied by [source receipts](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/source-hashes.json).
+
+R01 actual commands use pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` via `scripts/dev.ps1`, isolated `APPDATA` under `build/rivalry-social-share-*`, disabled backend URLs and unique fixture saves. Engine commands below use `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`, with normal host certificate/rendering access:
+
+- `python scripts/test_track_link_bridge.py --android-compile` — original Java link/text-sharing 22 checks and new image-sharing/provider/cache 34 checks, all passing. All three production Java classes compile against Android 36 and the pinned Godot AAR with Java release 17; [log](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/logs/android-bridge.log). No APK export.
+- `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_rivalry_share.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod gl_compatibility -TestArgument --evidence=res://../docs/evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/checked-gl_compatibility` — 358 checks, zero failures; [log](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/logs/checked-gl_compatibility.log).
+- The same focused test with `-RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan` and evidence directory `checked-mobile` — 358 checks, zero failures on the desktop Mobile renderer; [log](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/logs/checked-mobile.log).
+- `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_rivalry_share.gd` — 338 headless checks, zero failures; [log](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/logs/checked-test_rivalry_share.log).
+- `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_fault_dialog.gd` — 95 checks, zero failures; [log](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/logs/final-test_fault_dialog.log).
+- `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_app.gd` — 141 checks, zero failures; [log](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/logs/final-test_app.log).
+- `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd` — 906 scripts, zero failures; [log](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/logs/checked-test_script_parse.log).
+- `git diff --check -- game/core/app.gd game/ui/rivalry_share_dialog.gd game/platform/challenge_links.gd game/addons/bmt_challenges/export_plugin.gd native/challenges scripts/test_track_link_bridge.py game/tests/test_rivalry_share.gd` — passes, with the existing CRLF normalization warning.
+
+Focused cases include the real rendered PNG, its decoded dimensions/transparency, exact caption, bounded long-error feedback, first-tap native handoff, cached repeat shares, fresh request identities, retryable/stale native failures and held image completion across double taps, closing, account, car, week, group, cached/ownership and navigation changes. The export provider's manifest contract is checked without exporting an APK. Java tests run the actual bridge/provider/files against platform doubles, exercise URI reads and denials plus cache limits, and compile the production classes against the real Android/Godot libraries. These are not cross-app phone tests. No assertion or runtime check was weakened. Initial narrower runs are retained separately from the final expanded checks.
+
+G01 inspected artifacts:
+
+- [Actual shared PNG, Compatibility](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/checked-gl_compatibility/exported-results-card.png).
+- [Actual shared PNG, desktop Mobile](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/checked-mobile/exported-results-card.png).
+- [Desktop preview with Save image](evidence/rivalry-social-share-2026-10-19/checked-gl_compatibility/share-perfect-960x540.png).
+
+Platform references: Android's [sharing guidance](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/sharing/send) specifies the chooser and stream/text handoff; the [ContentProvider API](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/ContentProvider) supplies the read-only file interface; [manifest placeholders](https://developer.android.com/build/manage-manifests#inject_build_variables_into_the_manifest) supply the application-specific authority. The existing Godot v2 plugin and Android APIs are reused.
+
+Q01: owner appearance/workflow acceptance, actual Android chooser/WhatsApp/other-app handoff and the desktop native save dialog remain device/manual acceptance checks. Receiving apps decide how to use the supplied caption. No phone attachment check or physical-device test, APK/export/install, real social message, live account/backend mutation or deployment was performed. A matching future Android client build is required to use the new native method/provider; Windows direct sharing remains outside this implementation.
